    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can identify the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflectors on both sides to define the entry point and prevent responders from missing the turn.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and debris so fire apparatus and ambulances can reach the main residence without obstruction.\n• Maintain driveway width and overhead clearance along the entire length to allow large emergency vehicles to pass without stopping.\n• Identify a turnaround area near the main residence or detached structure where apparatus can reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Mark or post the turnaround location so arriving responders can locate it immediately.\n• Trim vegetation along both sides of the driveway that narrows the travel path or reduces visibility for drivers approaching the structures.\n• Cut back vegetation growing close to the main residence and detached structure so responders can move around the exterior of both buildings without obstruction.\n• Keep the walkway between the main residence and detached structure clear so responders can move quickly between the two buildings.\n• Post the property address on or near both structures if they are not visible from the driveway approach.\n• Keep any gates along the driveway unlocked or equipped with a Knox Box so responders are not delayed"
  },
