    "recommendations": "• Trim tree branches that hang over or touch the roof and walls of the structure.\n• Thin scattered trees close to the structure to create more open space between the canopy and the building.\n• Remove shrubs growing directly against the foundation or exterior walls.\n• Thin shrub clusters within close range of the structure to break up continuous vegetation surrounding the building.\n• Mow or cut the grass cover around the structure short, particularly during dry periods.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of overhanging branches to allow emergency vehicles to pass through without obstruction.\n• Mark the driveway entrance clearly so it is easy to locate quickly from the road.\n• Keep the driveway surface and shoulders clear of dead grass and loose plant debris that could carry fire along its length.\n• Maintain the open terrain areas around the structure by preventing shrub and grass growth from filling in and reducing the separation that currently exists."
